 "basis": "ELAPSED resource time since the VM was created, multiplied by list price. It is NOT an upper bound on compute, and it used to say it was: the justification given was that the VM had been deallocated for part of the window, but the subscription activity log for the whole window contains no deallocate or powerOff operation at all -- the VM was shut down from inside the guest OS, which holds the allocation and bills compute in full. Treat the VM line as the elapsed charge. The disks and the IP bill either way. The trial subscription reports pretaxCost: null for every meter, so no authoritative per-resource figure exists. SCOPE: the resources listed under `items` only. Blob storage is priced for DATA AT REST at the first Hot LRS tier, scaled by the --blob-bytes passed in; its transaction, egress and early-deletion meters are NOT priced, and neither is any resource outside the resource group -- notably the Cloud Shell file share, which a resource-group delete does not remove.",
